1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,040
Hey, judges. I'm Layken.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:05,290
I'm from Louisiana, and I've been hearing
about these big data centers

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,300
and SpaceX launch facilities proposed
around the state.

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:12,430
I wanted to read more about this and found
it hard to find sources that

5
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:15,240
I could trust. So I built Public Parish.

6
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:19,810
This is a free, open-source, nonpartisan
tool for keeping track of

7
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,160
Louisiana government decisions.

8
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:25,320
I'd like to show the Meta $50 billion data
center project.

9
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:29,990
Here on this page, we bring together what
the established record is.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
As well as the timeline of the project.

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,630
Everything here is built and generated on
top of official

12
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:42,290
source documentation from councils,
commissions, organizations related

13
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,140
to this project.

14
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:46,000
Everything stated here has citations.

15
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:51,430
We can open these, read the official
source or even link back to

16
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,680
the PDFs put out by the Louisiana Public
Service Commission.

17
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:00,460
Another cool thing we can do is ask about
this story.

18
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:05,150
So if we go here and we ask a question,
what happens if Meta ends its

19
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,460
service agreement early?

20
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:10,610
So what happens is our system is looking
at all the official

21
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:14,490
documentation in our database, searching
through them what is relevant

22
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:18,080
to your question, picking out the answer
and writing it for you.

23
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:22,560
And again, everything here, this gives us
an explanation and it's cited.

24
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:26,250
So we're able to open up the source and
verify the claims in this

25
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:30,640
answer. Another thing we can do with this
project is follow it through email.

26
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:35,270
So any material updates that come out
related to the Meta data center

27
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:38,220
will be sent to you as an update through
email.

28
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,680
Here's an update that I received recently.

29
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:45,910
Cool thing here is you can reply to the
email and this uses the same

30
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:50,390
functionality as the chat inside the
application and Public Parish

31
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:55,050
replies with the explanation as well as
the cited sources

32
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:57,360
to verify the claim.

33
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,670
We're launching today with support for
statewide stories as well as

34
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:03,460
three parishes here in Louisiana.

35
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:08,400
Users can select their home parish and
keep up with anything happening locally.

36
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:13,400
View issues, ask questions, and follow
anything here through email.

37
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:18,070
For the hackathon sponsors, Convex handles
our database authentication

38
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:22,530
and workflows. Firecrawl is for scraping
and monitoring

39
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,900
all of the official sources and documents.

40
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:29,620
OpenAI handles the reasoning, extraction,

41
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:34,530
and answers questions through the Convex
AI Gateway and AgentMail

42
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:38,970
handles everything from sending out update
emails as well as handling

43
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:42,120
the replies to user questions in email.

44
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,900
This is live today at publicparish.com.
